<!--
  Views/Controls/Segmented.xaml — B4 (Settings + Onboarding). Generic port of SettingsView.swift's
  private `Segmented<T>` (SettingsView.swift:817-849): a row of pill-shaped option buttons, one of
  which is selected. Swift's version is `<T: Hashable>`-generic; a WinUI UserControl cannot itself
  be generic, so this control operates over boxed `object` ids (see Segmented.xaml.cs's own header
  note) — exactly the same "bind through a raw id" convention SettingsView.swift ITSELF already
  falls back to for every non-Hashable enum it drives through this control (SpeechEngineChoice/
  ParseEnginePreference/Density all bind via `.rawValue`/a hand-picked string id per that file's own
  comments), so this is not a fidelity loss, just the same trick made structural.

  CornerRadius/Thickness gotcha (wave4-contract.md "Hard gotchas"): outer CornerRadius 8 and the
  0.5 BorderThickness are hand-copied literals (VolarHairlineThickness's value only, no matching
  outer-radius Metrics key — SettingsView.swift:846-847 uses a bare `cornerRadius: 8` one-off, same
  as Swift's own file). Inner option-button CornerRadius 6 matches Metrics.xaml's
  VolarCornerRadiusSmall VALUE but is still hand-copied (SettingsView.swift:839's own `cornerRadius:
  6, style: .continuous)` one-off) since CornerRadius cannot bind to a StaticResource.

  Background Color.black.opacity(0.25) (SettingsView.swift:845) -> alpha = round(0.25*255) = 63.75
  -> 64 = 0x40 -> #40000000 (same math this wave's other views already use for this exact literal —
  recurs 3x in SettingsView.swift per views-inventory.md SS1.15 point 4: this control's own bg, the
  long-press chip bg (Hotkeys tab), KeyRecorder's bg).
-->
<UserControl
    x:Class="Volar.App.Views.Controls.Segmented"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <Border
        x:Name="RootBorder"
        Padding="2"
        CornerRadius="8"
        BorderThickness="0.5"
        Background="#40000000"
        BorderBrush="{StaticResource VolarGlassBorderBrush}"
        HorizontalAlignment="Left">
        <StackPanel x:Name="OptionsPanel" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="0" />
    </Border>
</UserControl>
